  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## What listeners single out\n\n- Newer songs appear in semi-stripped down guitar and bass versions during the set [4]\n\n## Setlist highlights\n\n- **rules for the set**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [7]\n- **Going to Queens**: rare: 14 archived performances [7]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **tmg2004-03-03.flac8** (recommended): audience recording; 18 songs; 65 min; rated 3.8/5 by 5 [1]. Said about its sound: Audio is described as remarkably good, warm, and very crisp, avoiding a crappy sound; The recording is noted as being hard to listen to for the most part [1][6]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- John claims his voice was shot by the end, though the listener disagrees [4]\n- The show heats up significantly when the band adds drums to the performance [4]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **tmg2004-03-03.flac8**: source: AUD > battery box > Sony MD > Spin Doctor > CDR(m) [1]. Also: Taper used Sony Mini Disc recorder, Radio Shack mics, and Spin Doctor for transfer [1]",
